  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Designing the Cart Page**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the `src/pages/Cart.tsx` file and specifically, the dynamic free shipping progress bar. I\'ve noted the threshold for free shipping, which is 2,000,000 (that is 2,000). I\'m thinking how to visually represent the progress effectively within the cart page layout.\n\n\n**Calculating the Progress**\n\nI\'ve determined the approach for calculating the free shipping progress. I\'ll determine how much is left until free shipping and the progress percentage. I am using `Math.max(0, FREE_SHIPPING_THRESHOLD - cartTotal)` for the remaining amount, and `Math.min(100, Math.round((cartTotal / FREE_SHIPPING_THRESHOLD) * 100))` for percentage. I\'ve also implemented a boolean for checking if free shipping is achieved.\n\n\n**Implementing the UI**\n\nI\'m now focused on the UI elements for the free shipping progress. I\'m considering conditional rendering based on whether free shipping is achieved. I plan to use the amount remaining to inform the user about how close they are to free shipping. Also I plan to include a progress bar with dynamic width, and percentage display in RTL format. I\'m thinking of using a `motion.div` for the progress bar animation using `framer-motion`. I\'ll use a gradient fill when free shipping is reached.\n\n\n**Refining the Visuals**\n\nI\'m now iterating on the visual presentation of the free shipping progress bar. I\'m focusing on incorporating a shimmer or highlight effect for a modern aesthetic, and I\'m adding conditional styling based on free shipping status. I\'m aiming for a subtle glow or pulse when free shipping is activated. I am also updating the order summary sidebar, with dynamic text and icons to indicate free shipping status and add a badge or note to indicate free shipping threshold.\n\n\n"
